---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../data/site.js';
export function getStaticPaths() {
const pages = {
  project: {title:'About the Project', eyebrow:'01 / PROJECT', heading:'Understanding memory as part of disaster risk.', intro:'MNEMORISK examines how earthquake memories in Erzincan are experienced and transmitted, and how they relate to risk perception, preparedness and place attachment.', blocks:[
    ['Why memory?', 'The earthquakes of 1939 and 1992 left deep marks on the collective memory of Erzincan. Those who experienced the earthquakes, those who heard family accounts and those who moved to the city later may develop different relationships with these memories. The project explores how these differences shape risk assessments and preparedness.'],
    ['Research objective', 'MNEMORISK aims to examine disaster vulnerability not only through physical risk parameters and socioeconomic indicators, but also through social and individual factors such as collective memory, personal earthquake experiences and place attachment. Focusing on the urban centre of Erzincan, the research integrates engineering data with perceived-risk data shaped by past disaster experiences and collective memory in a Geographic Information Systems (GIS) environment. It compares the spatial distribution of physical hazard indicators and social risk perceptions and investigates potential mismatches between these dimensions. The findings are expected to contribute to understanding the cognitive and cultural dimensions of disaster vulnerability.'],
    ['Project details', 'Mnemonic Social Vulnerability: Integrating Collective Memory into Disaster Risk Management and Spatial Modelling in Erzincan, Türkiye. Conducted at Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University and awarded funding under the TÜBİTAK 1001 Programme (Project No. 226K193).']
  ]},
  research: {title:'Research Design',eyebrow:'02 / RESEARCH',heading:'A multi-method study of a city’s memory.',intro:'A three-stage research design combining household surveys, in-depth interviews and geographic information systems analysis.',blocks:[
    ['Methodology', 'MNEMORISK adopts a mixed-methods research design to examine the relationships between disaster risk, collective memory and place attachment through a multi-layered analytical framework. The study follows an explanatory sequential mixed-methods design, bringing quantitative and qualitative evidence together to investigate complex social processes.'],
    ['01 — Household survey', 'Face-to-face surveys are planned with 1,093 randomly selected households across 85 neighbourhoods in central Erzincan. The questionnaire covers earthquake experience, intergenerational narratives, risk perception, place attachment and preparedness. Quantitative data will be examined using statistical analysis.'],
    ['02 — In-depth interviews', 'Following the quantitative analysis, qualitative fieldwork will explore the survey findings in greater depth. Interviews will be conducted with earthquake witnesses, people who carry family memories and local stakeholders in selected neighbourhoods. Topics include disaster memory, risk perception, earthquake experience and place attachment.'],
    ['03 — Spatial modelling', 'Quantitative analyses will examine the factor structure, measurement model and relationships among variables. Qualitative and quantitative findings will then be integrated. Survey and interview findings will be considered alongside engineering data, including ground conditions, fault lines and building stock, in a GIS environment. Spatial layers will be developed to examine patterns of vulnerability, areas of concentration and potential mismatches between physical indicators and perceived risk.']
  ]},
  publications: {title:'Publications and News',eyebrow:'04 / PUBLICATIONS & NEWS',heading:'Research notes and project updates.',intro:'Articles, conference papers, reports, field notes and project announcements will be brought together here.',blocks:[
    ['Publication archive', 'Bibliographic details, open-access links and downloadable documents will be added as research outputs become available.'],
    ['Project updates', 'Updates on fieldwork, meetings and public events will be shared in this section.']
  ]},
  team: {title:'Research Team',eyebrow:'05 / TEAM',heading:'Research team.',intro:'The academic team and project scholars contributing to MNEMORISK.',members:[
    {name:'Assoc. Prof. Dr. Akın Bakioğlu',role:'Principal Investigator',institution:'Department of Sociology, Faculty of Arts and Sciences, Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University',image:'/akin-bakioglu.png',bio:[
      'Akın Bakioğlu is a faculty member in the Department of Sociology at the Faculty of Arts and Sciences, Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University. He completed his undergraduate and master’s degrees at Süleyman Demirel University and his PhD at Ankara University in 2019. Based on his doctoral dissertation, his book Büyük Madenci Yürüyüşü: Zonguldak’ın Büyük Grevi (1990–1991) was published by İletişim Publications in 2022.',
      'His academic work focuses primarily on the sociology of labour and class, as well as industrial sociology, migration, urban sociology, digital capitalism, platform labour, collective memory and disaster sociology. From a historical and critical sociological perspective, his research examines the relationships between the transformation of labour processes, class relations, spatial inequalities and social change.',
      'In 2024–2025, he conducted postdoctoral research in the Department of Sociology at the University of Tübingen, Germany, with support from the TÜBİTAK Postdoctoral Research Fellowship Programme. His fieldwork examined the working experiences, labour processes, class positions and organisational practices of workers of Turkish origin in Germany. He continues his national and international academic work and is a member of the Executive Board of the Turkish Sociological Association.'
    ]},
    {name:'Prof. Dr. Müzeyyen Aytül Kasapoğlu',role:'Researcher',institution:'Department of Sociology, Faculty of Arts and Sciences, Başkent University',image:'/MUZEYYEN%20AYT%C3%9CL%20KASAPO%C4%9ELU.png',bio:''},
    {name:'Assoc. Prof. Dr. Ahmet Emrah Siyavuş',role:'Researcher',institution:'Department of Geography, Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences, Marmara University',image:'/AHMET%20EMRAH%20S%C4%B0YAVU%C5%9E.png',bio:''},
    {name:'Assist. Prof. Dr. İlhan Zeynep Karakılıç',role:'Researcher',institution:'Department of Sociology, Bahçeşehir University',image:'/%C4%B0LHAN%20ZEYNEP%20KARAKILI%C3%87.png',bio:'Her research interests include rural sociology, migration sociology and memory studies.'},
    {name:'Yusuf Bulucu',role:'Project Scholar',institution:'Graduate student in Geography, Fırat University',image:'/YUSUF%20BULUCU.png',bio:'His research interests include disaster risk, GIS, remote sensing, spatial statistics and machine learning.'},
    {name:'Sümeyye Turak',role:'Project Scholar',institution:'Graduate student in Sociology, Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University',image:'/S%C3%9CMEYYE%20TURAK.png',bio:'Her research focuses on collective memory and disaster sociology.'}
  ],blocks:[]},
  contact: {title:'Contact',eyebrow:'06 / CONTACT',heading:'Get in touch with MNEMORISK.',intro:'For research enquiries, academic collaboration and institutional requests.',blocks:[
    ['Project correspondence', 'The project contact channels will be published here once the official details are finalised.'],
    ['Institutional affiliation', 'MNEMORISK is conducted at Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University, Türkiye.']
  ]}
};
return Object.keys(pages).map(slug => ({ params: { slug }, props: { page: pages[slug] } }));
}
const { page } = Astro.props;
---
<SiteLayout title={page.title} description={page.intro}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">{page.eyebrow}</span><h1>{page.heading}</h1><p>{page.intro}</p></header>
    {page.members ? (
      <section class="team-grid" aria-label="MNEMORISK research team">
        {page.members.map((member) => <details class="team-card">
          <summary class="team-card-trigger">
            <div class="team-card-photo">
              {member.image && <img src={member.image} alt={member.name} loading="lazy" />}
            </div>
            <div class="team-card-content">
              <div class="eyebrow">{member.role}</div>
              <h2>{member.name}</h2>
              <p class="team-institution">{member.institution}</p>
            </div>
          </summary>
          {member.bio && (
            <div class="team-bio">{Array.isArray(member.bio) ? member.bio.map(paragraph => <p>{paragraph}</p>) : <p>{member.bio}</p>}</div>
          )}
        </details>)}
      </section>
    ) : (
      <div class="article-list">
        {page.blocks.map((block) => <section class="article-row"><h2>{block[0]}</h2><p>{block[1]}</p></section>)}
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.wrap{width:min(1220px,calc(100% - 64px));margin-inline:auto}.team-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:30px 24px;padding:26px 0 80px}.team-card{min-width:0;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce5eb;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.team-card-trigger{display:flex;flex-direction:column;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;height:100%}.team-card-trigger::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.team-card-photo{height:260px;background:#edf2f5;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden;padding:12px}.team-card-photo img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}.team-card-content{padding:22px 22px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1}.team-card-content .eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;line-height:1.5;color:#668195;min-height:17px}.team-card-content h2{font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-weight:600;color:#1e4058;margin:9px 0 10px;min-height:54px}.team-institution{font:13px/1.65 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#63798a;margin:0 0 16px}.team-bio{padding:20px 20px 22px;border-top:1px solid #dce5eb}.team-bio p{font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.9;color:#465e6e;margin:0;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-word}.page-intro{padding:55px 0 38px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde5eb}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#4c7290}.page-intro h1{font-size:clamp(34px,3.9vw,51px);line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:13px 0 16px}.page-intro p{font-size:clamp(16px,1.45vw,19px);color:#596c7e;line-height:1.55;max-width:790px;margin:0}.article-list{padding:25px 0 60px}.article-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(210px,.9fr) 1.7fr;gap:35px;padding:31px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde5eb}.article-row h2{font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,30px);line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:8px 0}.article-row p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:#526577;margin:0}.button{display:inline-flex;background:#153c54;color:white;padding:14px 20px;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:65px}@media(max-width:900px){.team-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:22px}.team-card-photo{height:240px}}@media(max-width:560px){.team-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px;padding-top:18px}.team-card-photo{height:270px}.team-card-content{padding:20px}.team-card-content h2{min-height:0;font-size:20px}}@media(max-width:600px){.wrap{width:calc(100% - 32px)}.page-intro{padding:36px 0 28px}.article-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px;padding:23px 0}.article-row p{font-size:16px}}
</style>